          "id": "oral-history",
          "type": "audio",
          "importance": "supporting",
          "body": "The Inter-Civic Council and C. K. Steele\n\nThe Inter-Civic Council led the citywide Tallahassee bus boycott. Its elected president was Rev. C. K. Steele, pastor of Bethel Baptist Church. Students Wilhelmina Jakes and Carrie Patterson sparked the protest, and students and residents helped sustain it. The council called for seating on a first-come basis, courteous treatment and the hiring of Black drivers. Rev. Daniel B. Speed was among the other organizers who helped lead the campaign.",
