          "importance": "supporting",
          "body": "The boycott, month by month\n\nLate May 1956: The arrests of Jakes and Patterson prompt a student boycott. A community meeting votes to join it and forms the Inter-Civic Council.\nJuly–August 1956: Bus service stops and then returns. The operator hires Black drivers on the FAMU–Frenchtown run.\nOctober 1956: A municipal court convicts 21 people in connection with the boycott carpool. The boycott continues.\nJanuary 1957: The city repeals its explicit racial seating rule, replacing it with driver-assigned seating. Riders test the new rule.\nSummer 1957: Florida Memory dates integration of the city buses to this summer.",
